# tenant-vocabulary.baseline — the ratchet on tenant words above their
# tier, read by infra/lint/no-tenant-vocabulary-above-its-tier.sh
# (backlog be39298f). One line per FILE that still carries a word:
# `<count><TAB><path>`, in path order, one blank line apart.
#
# Each number is the lint's OWN measurement of that file, and it only
# goes down: the lint refuses a file whose count is above its line (the
# leak grew), a word in a file with no line (its baseline is 0), and a
# file whose count is below its line (set the line to the count in the
# same car — or delete it, at 0). Nobody raises one. The target is no
# lines at all.
#
# Per file since 2026-09-27 (backlog e889cfa4): it was one line per
# tier, and every car lowering apps/web/src rewrote the same integer,
# so parked cars conflicted with main on it after every train. A car
# now edits only the lines of the files it touched. The blank line
# between entries is load-bearing — git refuses two edits to adjacent
# lines — and the lint header says why. Written from
# `infra/lint/no-tenant-vocabulary-above-its-tier.sh --measure` on
# origin/main 89f22971, whose per-tier sums it reproduces exactly
# (crates/core 303, crates/modules 333, crates/orchestrators 789,
# apps/web/src 246, apps/simulator 9, infra/postgres/schema 175,
# infra/platform 2, infra/cluster 7). Regenerate the entries the same
# way; never type one.

